 \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting chain from 767 to 1635 satisfies the 600-unit inter-hop limit: under \u0394=600 only 4 nodes are reachable from 767 and no paths exist. The only ordered route (767\u2192722\u2192302\u21921635) requires waits of 611 and 27,350 units, and reachability still fails at \u0394=2000 and \u0394=10000. The apparent link is explained by static density and the hub status of intermediary 302 (167 events, 142 partners) rather than by prompt temporal propagation.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 40114, "total_output_tokens": 2970, "total_tokens": 43084, "total_latency_ms": 47929, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}